            {
                "entry_id": "a1b00af1-5ab4-3bc3-8583-476f51f5c175",
                "word": "cryptomorphique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6648e73b-a788-4bae-bdb8-80b1868de160",
                        "entry_id": "a1b00af1-5ab4-3bc3-8583-476f51f5c175",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "cryptomorphiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bdfe997f-7337-3eda-a10b-2940dc8eaa94",
                        "entry_id": "a1b00af1-5ab4-3bc3-8583-476f51f5c175",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Se dit de deux objets, et plus spécialement deux systèmes d’axiomes ou leurs sémantiques si et seulement s’ils sont équivalents mais pas de manière évidente."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "97f01615-8e2a-42b0-880d-58c678779e45",
                        "source_entry_id": "a1b00af1-5ab4-3bc3-8583-476f51f5c175",
                        "source_sense_id": "bdfe997f-7337-3eda-a10b-2940dc8eaa94",
                        "target_lang_word": "cryptomorphic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cryptomorphic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4dee1ed6-bbec-3928-b9bb-152ef3c7931f",
                                        "entry_id": "9ced31e3-d06c-3ddb-92d8-f1c13b50328c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Two objects, especially systems of axioms or semantics for them, are called cryptomorphic if they are equivalent (possibly in some informal sense) but not obviously equivalent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da0659ce-742e-4787-ba60-88c2cb4bc60c",
                                                "sense_id": "4dee1ed6-bbec-3928-b9bb-152ef3c7931f",
                                                "text": "Find them, and prove that an operation satisfying them provides another cryptomorphic version of topology 8."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32df2183-bd04-3ea2-8a6c-a4f1590bc6f8",
                                        "entry_id": "9ced31e3-d06c-3ddb-92d8-f1c13b50328c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a form that obscures or masks the underlying meaning or purpose."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "800801dc-a4ab-48fb-8576-8724cc2b4f5a",
                                                "sense_id": "32df2183-bd04-3ea2-8a6c-a4f1590bc6f8",
                                                "text": "Some degree of light may perhaps be thrown on the cryptomorphic condition of bodies in combination, by our knowledge of the typical conditions of natural bodies generally, when uncombined."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ce62500-3dec-4311-9be3-cd051a4ffa0d",
                                                "sense_id": "32df2183-bd04-3ea2-8a6c-a4f1590bc6f8",
                                                "text": "But there are two drawings and a painting that will be shown to be of Cézanne père and that have not been recognized as such — because he is without the hat he wears in the works mentioned above — as well as cryptomorphic portraits that are also hatless, all done, we may be sure, from memory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c50e8e5-8967-4a37-a919-370b54ff1fa2",
                                                "sense_id": "32df2183-bd04-3ea2-8a6c-a4f1590bc6f8",
                                                "text": "I can imagine, for example, constructing the argument that Poe's Purloined Letter is the locus classicus for all cryptomorphic revelations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d1c062f-511c-47ce-ab7c-047ffeeee516",
                                                "sense_id": "32df2183-bd04-3ea2-8a6c-a4f1590bc6f8",
                                                "text": "I call this image cryptomorphic because it hides as it reveals, unlike the skull in Holbein's “Ambassadors”; that is, this smeared film image does not reveal a hidden image behind the smear."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "29783721-6869-3ad9-be18-54a720e844ff",
                                        "entry_id": "9ced31e3-d06c-3ddb-92d8-f1c13b50328c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a cryptic structure in which the ultimate active product is carried by the precursorial protein rather than the protein actually encoded by the gene."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb24603a-0f27-48e5-8189-3ad82c12a791",
                                                "sense_id": "29783721-6869-3ad9-be18-54a720e844ff",
                                                "text": "Three types of genes, namely, immunoglobulin genes, dimorphic genes and cryptomorphic genes, are classified as complex genes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a66082-6126-40e0-aa6a-223fb98c51c2",
                                                "sense_id": "29783721-6869-3ad9-be18-54a720e844ff",
                                                "text": "Hence, among the lower vertebrates, the cistron may be diplomorphic rather than cryptomorphic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "216bdbed-0eda-3dc5-aa98-cff7c332fb0b",
                                        "entry_id": "9ced31e3-d06c-3ddb-92d8-f1c13b50328c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Found or occurring below the soil layer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62846012-98ee-4579-86ee-1ef24bd2ec57",
                                                "sense_id": "216bdbed-0eda-3dc5-aa98-cff7c332fb0b",
                                                "text": "Either the cryptomorphic silica replaced the microcrystalline dolomite, followed by mineralization or the reverse, in the order of silicification, is possible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4910db53-1756-438a-9f5b-4cfe1df0b5cf",
                                                "sense_id": "216bdbed-0eda-3dc5-aa98-cff7c332fb0b",
                                                "text": "Cryptomorphic biological soil crusts are the most difficult to observe and occur to a lesser known extent within the Planning Area ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57f82a51-6343-4807-8407-ef471715cf8c",
                                                "sense_id": "216bdbed-0eda-3dc5-aa98-cff7c332fb0b",
                                                "text": "The vertical flow of the substance may scatter and create dissipative cryptomorphic structures on the surface, which are poorly expressed in the relief."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb95f015-61c7-48a4-b1e6-9e44f8d44cc2",
                                                "sense_id": "216bdbed-0eda-3dc5-aa98-cff7c332fb0b",
                                                "text": "The first group includes surface phenomena (i.e. exomorphic, or superficial phenomena), and the second group comprises underground phenomena (i.e. cryptomorphic, or subficial phenomena)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78d4fc63-d43e-33e7-a380-a61a20f354c8",
                                        "entry_id": "9ced31e3-d06c-3ddb-92d8-f1c13b50328c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Composed of minerals that are not expressed in their crystalline form."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "caa48d42-b759-46d3-9183-a883ebf6d513",
                                                "sense_id": "78d4fc63-d43e-33e7-a380-a61a20f354c8",
                                                "text": "Both have 'cryptomorphic' types which are similar in composition but in which no felspar has crystallized."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
